        "theme":  "Philosophy",
        "summary":  "Research by Boston University professor Emma Wiles found that framing AI agents as \u0027employees\u0027 reduces human error detection by 18% and increases unwarranted delegation of responsibility. The study shows that marketing AI agents with human-like job titles and organizational personas creates false expectations that undermine human accountability. The concern is most acute as these systems expand into healthcare, warfare, and government contexts.",
