        "execSummary":  "Google DeepMind\u0027s $10 million bet on multi-agent safety research is an implicit acknowledgment that the industry is deploying agent systems faster than it understands the systemic risks they introduce. The concern is not individual agent misbehavior but emergent harms from millions of agents interacting — a category of risk that enterprise security teams have no established playbook for. CISOs and AI governance leads should treat this research investment as an early warning signal and begin mapping their agent deployment footprints against potential cross-agent attack surfaces. Building multi-agent safety requirements into vendor contracts and architecture reviews now is lower cost than retrofitting after incidents occur.",
